{"name":"The Goods","hex":"#aaa651","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"the goods","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person or an animal:\nActing in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral.","Acting in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/the_goods"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Goods (band)","blocks":[{"text":"The Goods were an American rock band formed in Miami, Florida, in 1989."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Goods_(band)"},{"title":"The Goods (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Goods was a Canadian daytime television talk show which aired on CBC Television from October 3, 2016 to May 10, 2018. Formatted as a lifestyle show, each of the four hosts specialized in a different subject area: Steven Sabados on home and design, Jessi Cruickshank on style and fashion, Andrea Bain on relationships and sexuality, and Shahir Massoud on food. The show was created as a replacement for Sabados' earlier CBC series Steven and Chris, which was cancelled in 2015 following the death of his husband and co-host Chris Hyndman."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/The_Goods_%28TV_series%29_logo.jpg/330px-The_Goods_%28TV_series%29_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Goods_(TV_series)"},{"title":"The Goods: Live Hard, Sell Hard","blocks":[{"text":"The Goods: Live Hard, Sell Hard is a 2009 American comedy film directed by Neal Brennan, produced by Adam McKay, Will Ferrell, Kevin Messick and Chris Henchy, written by Andy Stock and Rick Stempson and starring Jeremy Piven, Ving Rhames, James Brolin, David Koechner, Kathryn Hahn, Ed Helms, Jordana Spiro and Craig Robinson. Originally titled The Goods: The Don Ready Story, the film was theatrically released on August 14, 2009 in the United States by Paramount Pictures and was released on DVD as a rental only with no special features November 17 and for sale December 15. The film received mostly negative reviews from critics and grossed $15.3 million against a $10 million budget."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Goods_live_hard_sell_hard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Goods%3A_Live_Hard%2C_Sell_Hard"},{"title":"Goods","blocks":[{"text":"In certain economic contexts, goods are anything that is good, usually in the sense that it provides welfare or utility to someone. Goods can be contrasted with bads, i.e. things that provide negative value for users, like chores or waste products. A bad lowers a consumer's overall welfare."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Mediq_Sverige_Kungsbacka_warehouse.jpg/330px-Mediq_Sverige_Kungsbacka_warehouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goods"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Mate_mit_St%C3%A4ngeln.jpg/500px-Mate_mit_St%C3%A4ngeln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Mate_mit_St%C3%A4ngeln.jpg/500px-Mate_mit_St%C3%A4ngeln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMate_mit_St%C3%A4ngeln.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Coffee_Beans_Photographed_in_Macro.jpg/500px-Coffee_Beans_Photographed_in_Macro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Coffee_Beans_Photographed_in_Macro.jpg/1280px-Coffee_Beans_Photographed_in_Macro.jpg?ut